.TH PHASORSTD_DATA 3 "August 2026" "Phasor 4.0.0" "Phasor Standard Library 4.0.0"
.SH NAME
phasorstd_data \- Phasor encoding and hashing functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBinclude "std/data";\fR
.PP
.B base64_encode(input, url_safe)
.B base64_decode(data)
.B md5(input)
.B sha1(input)
.B sha256(input)
.PP
.B base64_encode_native(handle)
.B base64_decode_native(data)
.B md5_native(handle)
.B sha1_native(handle)
.B sha256_native(handle)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This module provides encoding/decoding, hashing, potentially home to cryptographic functions 
in the future. Each function has a simple string-based form (documented under FUNCTIONS) and
.B ManagedMemory
the native form (see \fBphasorstd_mem\fR(3) for the \fBManagedMemory\fR type) that
operates directly on a heap allocation instead of a Phasor string, for hashing or encoding
actual data.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BR base64_encode (input, url_safe)
Base64-encode a string.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBinput\fR 12
String to encode
.IP \fBurl_safe\fR 12
Boolean; if true, uses the URL- and filename-safe Base64 alphabet (\fB\-\fR and \fB_\fR in
place of \fB+\fR and \fB/\fR) instead of standard Base64
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Base64-encoded string
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBinput\fR is not a string or \fBurl_safe\fR is not a boolean
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR base64_decode (data)
Decode a Base64-encoded string.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
Base64-encoded string (standard or URL-safe alphabet)
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
The decoded string
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBdata\fR is not a string
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR md5 (input)
Compute the MD5 digest of a string.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBinput\fR 12
String to hash
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
32-character lowercase hexadecimal MD5 digest
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBinput\fR is not a string
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR sha1 (input)
Compute the SHA-1 digest of a value.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBinput\fR 12
String, integer, or float to hash. A string is hashed as its text bytes; an integer or float
is hashed as the raw bytes of its in-memory representation (platform-dependent size and
endianness), not as the text of its decimal representation.
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
40-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA-1 digest, or an empty string if \fBinput\fR is a type
other than string, integer, or float (e.g.\& boolean, array, struct, or null)
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR sha256 (input)
Compute the SHA-256 digest of a value.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBinput\fR 12
String, integer, or float to hash, with the same string-vs-numeric hashing rules as
\fBsha1()\fR
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
64-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 digest, or an empty string if \fBinput\fR is a
type other than string, integer, or float
.RE
.SH NATIVE MEMORY VARIANTS
These operate on a \fBManagedMemory\fR handle (see \fBphasorstd_mem\fR(3)) instead of a
Phasor string, hashing or transcoding the raw bytes of the allocation directly.
.TP
.BR md5_native (handle)
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
32-character lowercase hexadecimal MD5 digest of the \fBhandle.size\fR bytes at
\fBhandle.ptr\fR
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR sha1_native (handle)
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
40-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA-1 digest of the \fBhandle.size\fR bytes at
\fBhandle.ptr\fR
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR sha256_native (handle)
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
64-character lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 digest of the \fBhandle.size\fR bytes at
\fBhandle.ptr\fR
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR base64_encode_native (handle)
Intended to Base64-encode the raw bytes of a \fBManagedMemory\fR allocation.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Base64-encoded string of the \fBhandle.size\fR bytes at \fBhandle.ptr\fR, using the standard
(non-URL-safe) alphabet
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR base64_decode_native (data)
Intended to decode a Base64 string into a newly allocated \fBManagedMemory\fR buffer.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
Base64-encoded string
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle over a new heap allocation holding the decoded bytes; must be
released with \fBfree_native()\fR (see \fBphasorstd_mem\fR(3)) when no longer needed
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Base64
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/data";

var encoded: string = base64_encode("hello, world", false);
puts(encoded);                    // "aGVsbG8sIHdvcmxk"
puts(base64_decode(encoded));     // "hello, world"
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Hashing
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/data";

puts(md5("hello"));      // 5d41402abc4b2a76b9719d911017c592
puts(sha1("hello"));     // aaf4c61ddcc5e8a2dabede0f3b482cd9aea9434d
puts(sha256("hello"));   // 2cf24dba5fb0a30e26e83b2ac5b9e29e1b161e5c1fa7425e73043362938b9824

// Hashing a number hashes its raw bytes, not its printed digits
puts(sha256(42));
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
.B md5()
requires a string and throws on any other type;
.BR sha1() " and " sha256()
instead accept string, integer, or float and silently return an empty string for any other
type (boolean, array, struct, null) \(em check the return value if the input type is not
guaranteed to be one of these three
.IP \(bu 2
Hashing an integer or float hashes the raw bytes of its native representation, which is
platform- and build-dependent; if you need a stable, portable hash of a number, convert it to
a string first and hash that instead (e.g.\& \fBsha256(to_string(42))\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
.B base64_encode()
requires the \fBurl_safe\fR argument explicitly; there is no default
.IP \(bu 2
All hash digests are returned as lowercase hexadecimal strings
